# A declared tag on a literal is proven from its entries when every entry
# is a numeric literal (a number, with or without a unit, maybe negated).
S: Symmetric Matrix[2, 2] = [[2, 1], [1, 2]]
D: Diagonal Matrix[3, 3] = [[1, 0, 0], [0, -2, 0], [0, 0, 3]]
P: PositiveDefinite Matrix[2, 2] = [[4, 1], [1, 3]]
K: PositiveDefinite Matrix[2, 2] N/m = [[3000 N/m, -1000 N/m], [-1000 N/m, 2 kN/m]]
Z: Symmetric Diagonal Matrix[2, 2] = [[0, 0], [0, 0]]
